        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "The Bank Graph Notebook is meant to be used alongside this [Livelab](https://apexapps.oracle.com/pls/apex/r/dbpm/livelabs/run-workshop?p210_wid=770&p210_wec=&session=112325984461564).",
          "The Livelab has steps to automate the creation of a new Autonomous AI Database instance with the data required to create the bank_graph and walks you through the steps of creating the graph.",
          "Once you create bank_graph by following the steps in the Livelab, you can use this notebook to view and understand how graphs are used to identify circular and suspicious bank transactions.",
          "**Note**: You will get an error message if you have not created the bank_graph before running these paragraphs."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : {
          "startTime" : 1684956018883,
          "endTime" : 1684956019071,
          "interpreter" : "md",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<p>The Bank Graph Notebook is meant to be used alongside this <a href=\"https://apexapps.oracle.com/pls/apex/r/dbpm/livelabs/run-workshop?p210_wid=770&p210_wec=&session=112325984461564\">Livelab</a>.</p><p>The Livelab has steps to automate the creation of a new Autonomous AI Database instance with the data required to create the bank_graph and walks you through the steps of creating the graph.</p><p>Once you create bank_graph by following the steps in the Livelab, you can use this notebook to view and understand how graphs are used to identify circular and suspicious bank transactions.</p><p><strong>Note</strong>: You will get an error message if you have not created the bank_graph before running these paragraphs.</p>",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "First, load the graph into the in-memory graph server if it still needs to be loaded since we will execute some graph algorithms.",
          "",
          "Run the first %python-pgx paragraph, which uses the built-in session object to read the graph into memory from the database and creates a PgXGraph object that handles the loaded graph."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : {
          "startTime" : 1684956018883,
          "endTime" : 1684956019071,
          "interpreter" : "md",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<p>First, load the graph into the in-memory graph server if it still needs to be loaded since we will execute some graph algorithms.</p>\n<p>Run the first %python-pgx paragraph, which uses the built-in session object to read the graph into memory from the database and creates a PgXGraph object that handles the loaded graph.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%python-pgx",
          "",
          "GRAPH_NAME=\"BANK_GRAPH\"",
          "# try getting the graph from the in-memory graph server",
          "graph = session.get_graph(GRAPH_NAME)",
          "# if it does not exist read it into memory",
          "if (graph == None) :",
          "    session.read_graph_by_name(GRAPH_NAME, \"PG_PGQL\")",
          "    print(\"Graph \"+ GRAPH_NAME + \" successfully loaded\")",
          "    graph = session.get_graph(GRAPH_NAME)",
          "else :",
          "    print(\"Graph '\"+ GRAPH_NAME + \"' already loaded\")"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "raw",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : false,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
