        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "Next, execute the paragraph that queries and displays 100 graph elements.",
          "",
          "This PGQL query fetches the first 100 elements of the graph and displays them.",
          "The **MATCH** clause specifies a graph pattern.",
          "",
          "- (s) is the source node",
          "",
          "- [t] is an edge",
          "",
          "- -> indicates the edge direction, that is, from the source s to a destination d",
          "",
          "- (d) is the destination node",
          "",
          "The **LIMIT** clause specifies the maximum of elements that the query should return.",
          "",
          "See the [PGQL site](https://pgql-lang.org/) and specification for more details on the syntax and features of the language.",
          "The Getting Started notebook folder also has a tutorial on PGQL."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : {
          "startTime" : 1684956033547,
          "endTime" : 1684956033615,
          "interpreter" : "md",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<p>Next, execute the paragraph that queries and displays 100 graph elements.</p>\n<p>This PGQL query fetches the first 100 elements of the graph and displays them.\nThe <strong>MATCH</strong> clause specifies a graph pattern.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>(s) is the source node</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>[t] is an edge</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>-&gt; indicates the edge direction, that is, from the source s to a destination d</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>(d) is the destination node</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <strong>LIMIT</strong> clause specifies the maximum of elements that the query should return.</p>\n<p>See the <a href=\"https://pgql-lang.org/\">PGQL site</a> and specification for more details on the syntax and features of the language.\nThe Getting Started notebook folder also has a tutorial on PGQL.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
