          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<p>The fraud department has now also confirmed that <strong>934</strong> and <strong>387</strong> might have been involved in illegal activities. Chances are that accounts that received money from accounts <strong>934</strong> or 387 have also been part of the scheme, and maybe the accounts that received money from them. The &quot;closer&quot; an account is to 934 or 387, the higher the risk.\nWe use the <strong>Personalized PageRank algorithm</strong>, which computes <strong>PageRank</strong> values relative to a collection of vertices, which in this case is <strong>934</strong> and <strong>387</strong>.\nWe use the Python API again.\nThe code snippet uses the PgxGraph object graph containing a handle to the BANK_GRAPH we got earlier.\nIt invokes the <strong>Personalized PageRank</strong> algorithm with the built-in analyst Python object.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
